WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:05.400
"John Wick: Chapter 4" blasts its&nbsp;
way into theaters on March 24, 2023,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.100
and the people who have seen it say it's, well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:13.020
a blast. Though they also have a few minor&nbsp;
quibbles about the assassin's latest outing.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:17.580
The next "John Wick" movie looms ever closer,&nbsp;
and it looks like it's going to be another hit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:23.280
for Keanu Reeves' titular assassin. Expectations&nbsp;
for the movie have been sky-high, bolstered by a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:27.780
set of trailers and teases that suggest this&nbsp;
latest outing may be the most thrill-packed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:33.240
entry in the series yet. Even Reeves himself has&nbsp;
gone on record to say that "John Wick: Chapter 4"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:38.340
blows away everything that's come before in terms&nbsp;
of its action sequences. That's a very high bar.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:43.560
"'John Wick: Chapter 4'! This movie is crazy!"

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:48.180
With such sky-high expectations, some&nbsp;
may find themselves worried that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.080
flick isn't going to live up to the hype.&nbsp;
After all, it's a lot of pressure to put on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:57.180
the fourth entry in a blockbuster franchise.&nbsp;
All you have to do is look at 2022's "Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:02.040
Love and Thunder" to know that fourth entries&nbsp;
sometimes suffer from diminishing returns.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.920
But despite these concerns,&nbsp;
it seems that nervous fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:09.120
have nothing to fear. Critics who attended&nbsp;
early pre-release screenings of "John Wick:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:13.620
Chapter 4" have a lot of good things to say&nbsp;
about the upcoming flick. CinemaBlend's Eric&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.580
Eisenberg tweeted that he was pleased to&nbsp;
find that despite "John Wick: Chapter 4"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:22.320
being the longest movie in the franchise&nbsp;
yet, its extended runtime feels warranted.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:26.700
"It's an epic with smart pacing that&nbsp;
never lets the action feel exhausting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.680
and the set pieces are phenomenal."

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:33.540
Fandango's Erik Davis was similarly&nbsp;
impressed by the film's level of quality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:37.020
particularly in its action&nbsp;
sequences. Davis tweeted,

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:40.860
"This is definitely the biggest&nbsp;
&amp; most badass 'JOHN WICK' movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:45.420
yet [with] a runtime near 3 hours &amp; an&nbsp;
ending everyone will be talking about.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:50.940
No one does action like this – it's on&nbsp;
another level. Part 4 simply rules."

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.340
Beyond the stellar action sequences, critics&nbsp;
have also heaped praise on the movie's cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:59.460
which features a mix of series&nbsp;
veterans and newcomers to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:02.940
franchise. Critic Matt Neglia&nbsp;
of Next Best Picture wrote,

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:07.440
"Keanu Reeves continues to push his body&nbsp;
to the limit while Donnie Yen &amp; Hiroyuki&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.980
Sanada add real gravitas to the most&nbsp;
epic film of the franchise yet."

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:15.540
But even with all those positive reactions,&nbsp;
there are also a fair few critics out there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:20.640
that feel the movie falls short in some minor&nbsp;
regards. Total Film's Jordan Farley found the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.780
film's action to be a little excessive&nbsp;
and a touch too over the top, writing,

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:29.040
"Moment to moment fight choreography is as&nbsp;
thrilling as ever but the set-pieces don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.580
have enough variety to sustain&nbsp;
their jumbo size. Wick's 'Looney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:36.000
Tunes' pratfalls stretch credulity,&nbsp;
even in a world this heightened."

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:43.080
"Well, it looks like we have ourselves a…a&nbsp;
genuine conundrum. A quandary, if you will."

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:49.200
Others have griped a bit about the film's&nbsp;
length. Critic Sean Mulvihill mostly said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:54.360
good things, but noted it went on too long.&nbsp;
Variety's Simon Thompson called "John Wick:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:58.440
Chapter 4" "exhilarating as it is&nbsp;
exhausting." It seems those hoping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:03.000
for a breezy action flick may find the&nbsp;
scope and scale of the film overwhelming.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:06.420
Perhaps the most intriguing critique&nbsp;
of "John Wick: Chapter 4," however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:10.740
has to do with the ending. Based on&nbsp;
early reactions, it seems the film goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:15.600
in an unexpected direction as it reaches its&nbsp;
conclusion. Insider's Kirsten Acuna predicted:

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:19.200
"Lots of surprises in this one that's&nbsp;
going to deliver a divisive ending."

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.800
Nonetheless, a fifth "John Wick"&nbsp;
installment is confirmed to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.960
on the way, so make of that warning what you will.

